.policy "fastapi-practice-sync-session-in-async-route" revision 1
.description "Keep sync SQLAlchemy session work out of async FastAPI routes, dependencies, middleware and the helpers they call; use def, an AsyncSession or run_in_threadpool."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. FastAPI runs a `def` route or dependency in its threadpool and an `async def` one on
// the event loop, so a blocking query on a sync SQLAlchemy/SQLModel session written in, or reached from, an
// `async def` that FastAPI calls per request (a route, a dependency, HTTP middleware) stalls every concurrent request
// for its duration. It reports, outside test code, in such an async def's own frame (not a nested def or lambda) and
// not awaited:
//   - SessionCallInAsync: a blocking session method (ss_blocking: query, execute, scalars, scalar, get, commit,
//     flush, refresh, rollback, delete, merge, exec, close, remove) called on a sync session: a parameter holding
//     the request's session (lib/fastapi's fa_session_param: annotated `Session`, through Annotated or an alias such
//     as `SessionDep`, or filled by a dependency that yields a sync session), a session the function opens
//     (`with SessionLocal() as s`, `s = SessionLocal()`, `s = open_session()` where `open_session` is a sync def
//     annotated `-> Session` or returning one, `with session_scope() as s` for a @contextmanager yielding one),
//     `request.state.<x>` when the run assigns a sync session to `<anything>.state.<x>`, or a class attribute
//     holding one (`Trade.session`, `self.session`). In a chain (`db.query(User).filter(...).all()`) only the root
//     call on the session is reported.
//   - SessionReached: a call whose target (python/calls, across files) is surely a sync def that runs such work on a
//     sync session it receives (a parameter annotated as one, or one a caller passes a session to, positionally or by
//     keyword), opens itself, or reads from an attribute holding one, directly or through further sync defs. It
//     names the first session call it reaches.
//   routes.py:  async def r(db=Depends(get_db)): db.query(User).all()          reported at db.query
//   crud.py:    def get_users(db: Session): return db.query(User).all()
//   routes.py:  async def r(db=Depends(get_db)): return get_users(db)        reported at get_users(db)
//   main.py:    @app.middleware("http") ... request.state.db.commit()        reported, when request.state.db = SessionLocal()
// Left alone: a `def` route or dependency (the threadpool); an AsyncSession and awaited calls; work handed to
// `run_in_threadpool`, `asyncio.to_thread`, `anyio.to_thread.run_sync` or `loop.run_in_executor` (the helper is an
// argument, not a call) or written in a nested def or lambda; `db.add()`, `add_all()`, `expunge()`, which do no IO;
// an async helper (calling one only makes a coroutine); a call whose target is unknown (call_open); a `Session`
// from another library (`requests.Session`), told apart by its import; test files.
//   routes.py:  async def r(db=Depends(get_db)): return await run_in_threadpool(get_users, db)    not reported
//   routes.py:  def r(db=Depends(get_db)): return get_users(db)                                  not reported
// Gaps: a session reached through a value the call program or this rule cannot follow (a property or
// cached_property returning a repository built on the session, a session held in a container); an `async def`
// helper that is awaited and does sync session work inside (it is not a start: only per-request functions are);
// blocking calls that are not session methods (`inspect(engine)`, `engine.connect()`, sleep, HTTP), which
// python-practice-blocking-call-reached-from-async owns for the framework-free ones.

#include "lib/fastapi.rerail"
#include "python/calls.rerail"
#include "python/types.rerail"

// Whether an expression holds a sync session is a question over the run's files: the session may come from a
// dependency, an alias, a maker, a helper's return, a class attribute or a caller in another module (decision 0691: no
// node crosses files). Each file states its expressions' sessions under a condition (ss_ec, ss_mk, ss_ty: settled
// there, or naming another file's def, class, parameter or variable by symbol), the relations over symbols below
// settle the conditions (ss_ok), and the call graph is walked over defs' symbols (python/calls' call_target). A
// finding reads its call's node in its own file; SessionReached names the session call it reaches by path and line.
.violation SessionCallInAsync(at: node, what: symbol, fx: symbol)
    "`{what}` blocks the event loop inside `async def {fx}`. Make `{fx}` a plain `def` if it awaits nothing and sets no ContextVar; otherwise use an `AsyncSession` or `await run_in_threadpool(...)`."
SessionCallInAsync(o, what, fx) :- ss_work(o, f, what, c1, c2, c3), ss_ok(c1, c2, c3), pt_def(f, fq),
    ss_async_start(fq), def_name(f, fx).
.violation SessionReached(at: node, x: symbol, fx: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number)
    "`{x}()` runs sync session work (`{what}` at {p}:{l}) on the event loop in `async def {fx}`. Make `{fx}` a plain `def` if it awaits nothing; else `await run_in_threadpool({x}, ...)`."
SessionReached(c, x, fx, what, p, l) :- ss_frame_call(f, c), pt_def(f, fq), ss_async_start(fq), ss_tgt(c, g),
    ss_sync(g), ss_first(g, what, p, l), def_name(f, fx), field(c, "function", fn), text(fn, x).
SessionReached(c, x, fx, what, p, l) :- ss_frame_call(f, c), pt_def(f, fq), ss_async_start(fq),
    ss_prop_site(c, kq, pp, m), ss_prop_target(kq, pp, m, g), ss_sync(g), ss_first(g, what, p, l), def_name(f, fx),
    field(c, "function", fn), text(fn, x).

// ss_stop: code in a nested def, lambda or class runs later, not in the frame that writes it.
.decl ss_stop(k: symbol)
ss_stop("function_definition"). ss_stop("lambda"). ss_stop("class_definition").

// ss_async_start(f): async def f, outside test code, that FastAPI calls per request (lib/fastapi's fa_per_request: a
// route in any of its forms, a route registered by calling the decorator, `app.get("/x")(f)`, included). ss_async_def
// states the def's half in its file.
.decl ss_async_def(f: symbol)
ss_async_def(fq) :- kind(f, "function_definition"), is_async(f), docof(f, d), !fa_test_doc(d), pt_def(f, fq).
.decl ss_async_start(f: symbol)
ss_async_start(fq) :- fa_per_request(fq), ss_async_def(fq).

// ss_frame_call(f, c): call c, in def f's own frame, not awaited. ss_tgt(c, g): the call program surely calls g (no
// unknown target). ss_start_at(f, g): by symbols, what ss_start reads.
.decl ss_frame_call(f: node, c: node)
ss_frame_call(f, c) :- kind(c, "call"), nearest(c, f, ss_stop), kind(f, "function_definition"), !awaited(c).
.decl ss_tgt(c: node, g: symbol)
ss_tgt(c, g) :- kind(c, "call"), !call_open(c), call_target(c, g).
.decl ss_start_at(f: symbol, g: symbol)
ss_start_at(fq, g) :- ss_frame_call(f, c), ss_tgt(c, g), pt_def(f, fq).
.decl ss_start_prop(f: symbol, k: symbol, p: symbol, m: symbol)
ss_start_prop(fq, kq, pp, m) :- ss_frame_call(f, c), ss_prop_site(c, kq, pp, m), pt_def(f, fq).
// ss_start(g): an async start's call surely calls the sync def g: the call program's only answers, or, where it has
// none, a method reached through a property (ss_prop_target).
.decl ss_start(g: symbol)
ss_start(g) :- ss_start_at(fq, g), ss_async_start(fq), ss_sync(g).
ss_start(g) :- ss_start_prop(fq, kq, pp, m), ss_prop_target(kq, pp, m, g), ss_async_start(fq), ss_sync(g).
.decl ss_sync(g: symbol)
ss_sync(gq) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), !is_async(g), pt_def(g, gq).
// ss_reach(g, h): from start g, the sync def h runs in the same thread: g, or a call in a reached def's own frame
// (ss_edge, ss_prop_edge: stated in the calling def's file).
.decl ss_reach(g: symbol, h: symbol)
ss_reach(g, g) :- ss_start(g).
ss_reach(g, h) :- ss_reach(g, x), ss_edge(x, h), ss_sync(h).
ss_reach(g, h) :- ss_reach(g, x), ss_prop_edge(x, kq, pp, m), ss_prop_target(kq, pp, m, h), ss_sync(h).
.decl ss_edge(x: symbol, h: symbol)
ss_edge(xq, h) :- kind(c, "call"), call_target(c, h), nearest(c, x, ss_stop), kind(x, "function_definition"),
    pt_def(x, xq).
.decl ss_prop_edge(x: symbol, k: symbol, p: symbol, m: symbol)
ss_prop_edge(xq, kq, pp, m) :- ss_prop_site(c, kq, pp, m), nearest(c, x, ss_stop), kind(x, "function_definition"),
    pt_def(x, xq).
// ss_first(g, what, p, l): the session work reached from start g that SessionReached names: in the reached def of the
// least symbol, its first work (ss_work_ok: the i-th work of def h, counted in h's own order so an edit elsewhere in
// the file moves nothing, at line l of path p, which only the message reads, whose condition holds).
.decl ss_work_at(h: symbol, i: number, p: symbol, l: number, what: symbol, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_work_at(hq, i, p, l, what, c1, c2, c3) :- ss_work(o, h, what, c1, c2, c3), visit_index(o, v),
    i = count : { ss_work(o2, h, _, _, _, _), visit_index(o2, v2), v2 < v }, pt_def(h, hq), line(o, l), docof(o, d),
    doc(d, p, _).
.decl ss_work_ok(h: symbol, i: number, p: symbol, l: number, what: symbol)
ss_work_ok(hq, i, p, l, what) :- ss_work_at(hq, i, p, l, what, c1, c2, c3), ss_ok(c1, c2, c3).
.decl ss_hit(g: symbol, h: symbol)
ss_hit(g, h) :- ss_reach(g, h), ss_work_ok(h, _, _, _, _).
.decl ss_later_hit(g: symbol, h: symbol)
ss_later_hit(g, h) :- ss_hit(g, h), ss_hit(g, h2), h2 < h.
.decl ss_first(g: symbol, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number)
ss_first(g, what, p, l) :- ss_hit(g, h), !ss_later_hit(g, h), i = min j : { ss_work_ok(h, j, _, _, _) },
    ss_work_ok(h, i, p, l, what).

// ss_prop_site(c, k, p, m): c is `r.p.m(...)` where the type program proves r an instance of class k and the call
// program has no target. ss_prop_target(k, p, m, g): p is a property or cached_property of k whose return annotation
// names a class q of the run, and q's method m is g (`repos.users.get_one(...)` with `@cached_property def users(self)
// -> RepositoryUsers`). The call program leaves such calls open.
.decl ss_prop_site(c: node, k: symbol, p: symbol, m: symbol)
ss_prop_site(c, kq, pp, m) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, pe, m), attr_of(pe, r, pp),
    proven_type(r, kq), !call_target(c, _).
.decl ss_prop_target(k: symbol, p: symbol, m: symbol, g: symbol)
ss_prop_target(kq, pp, m, g) :- ss_prop_need(kq, pp, m), ss_meth(kq, pp, pd), ss_prop_ret(pd, q), ss_meth(q, m, g).
.decl ss_prop_need(k: symbol, p: symbol, m: symbol)
ss_prop_need(kq, pp, m) :- ss_prop_site(_, kq, pp, m).
// ss_prop_ret(pd, q): def pd is a property or cached_property whose return annotation names q, or a parametrized q
// (`Repo[User]`). Stated in its file.
.decl ss_prop_ret(pd: symbol, q: symbol)
ss_prop_ret(pdq, q) :- ss_property(pd), field(pd, "return_type", rt0), fa_strip(rt0, rt), ss_class_of(rt, q),
    pt_def(pd, pdq).
.decl ss_property(pd: node)
ss_property(pd) :- decorator(pd, e), unparen(e, d), (sym_of(d, "property") ; sym_of(d, "builtins.property") ;
    sym_of(d, "functools.cached_property")).
.decl ss_class_of(t: node, q: symbol)
ss_class_of(t, q) :- sym_of(t, q).
ss_class_of(t, q) :- fa_sub(t, q).
// ss_super(q, b): class q inherits from b, also through a parametrized base (`class R(Repo[User])`), which
// python/names' class_base does not read. ss_meth(q, m, g): q's method m is def g, its own or, if none, an ancestor's
// (python/names' mro_method, over ss_super, by symbol). ss_base and ss_own_meth are stated in the class's file.
.decl ss_base(q: symbol, b: symbol)
ss_base(q, b) :- class_def(c, q), class_base(c, b).
ss_base(q, b) :- class_def(c, q), field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, e, _), fa_sub(e, b).
.decl ss_super(q: symbol, b: symbol)
ss_super(q, b) :- ss_base(q, b).
ss_super(q, b) :- ss_super(q, m), ss_base(m, b).
.decl ss_own_meth(q: symbol, m: symbol, g: symbol)
ss_own_meth(q, m, gq) :- method(q, m, g), pt_def(g, gq).
.decl ss_has_meth(q: symbol, m: symbol)
ss_has_meth(q, m) :- ss_own_meth(q, m, _).
.decl ss_meth(q: symbol, m: symbol, g: symbol)
ss_meth(q, m, g) :- ss_own_meth(q, m, g).
ss_meth(q, m, g) :- ss_super(q, b), ss_own_meth(b, m, g), !ss_has_meth(q, m).

// ---- session work ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ss_blocking(m): Session methods that do IO (a query, a flush, a connection's commit, rollback or release).
// `remove` is scoped_session's: it closes the current session.
.decl ss_blocking(m: symbol)
ss_blocking("query"). ss_blocking("execute"). ss_blocking("scalars"). ss_blocking("scalar"). ss_blocking("get").
ss_blocking("commit"). ss_blocking("flush"). ss_blocking("refresh"). ss_blocking("rollback"). ss_blocking("delete").
ss_blocking("merge"). ss_blocking("exec"). ss_blocking("close"). ss_blocking("remove").
// ss_work(o, h, what, c1, c2, c3): call o, in def h's own frame and not awaited, is a blocking method on a sync
// session, under condition (c1, c2, c3).
.decl ss_work(o: node, h: node, what: symbol, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_work(o, h, cat(rt, ".", m, "()"), c1, c2, c3) :- ss_recv(o, r, m), ss_ec(r, c1, c2, c3), nearest(o, h, ss_stop),
    kind(h, "function_definition"), !awaited(o), text(r, rt).
.decl ss_recv(o: node, r: node, m: symbol)
ss_recv(o, r, m) :- kind(o, "call"), field(o, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, r0, m), ss_blocking(m), unparen(r0, r).

// ---- conditions --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A per-file relation states a session under a condition (c1, c2, c3), which ss_ok settles over symbols:
//   ("sure", "", "")      settled in its file
//   ("name", h, x)        name x of def h holds a sync session (ss_name_ok)
//   ("attr", k, a)        class k, or a base, has attribute a holding one (ss_class_attr)
//   ("state", a, "")      the run assigns one to `<x>.state.a` (ss_state_ok)
//   ("type", q, "")       q, a variable of another module, is a sync session type alias (lib/fastapi's fa_var_session)
//   ("maker", q, "")      q, a variable of another module, is a sync session maker (lib/fastapi's fa_var_maker)
//   ("ret", g, "")        g, a sync def a call surely calls, gives a sync session (ss_returns_ok)
//   ("retcm", g, "")      the same for a @contextmanager def, whose call stays open
.decl ss_ok(c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_ok("sure", "", "").
ss_ok("name", h, x) :- ss_name_ok(h, x).
ss_ok("attr", k, a) :- ss_class_attr(k, a).
ss_ok("state", a, "") :- ss_state_ok(a).
ss_ok("type", q, "") :- fa_var_session(q, "sync").
ss_ok("maker", q, "") :- fa_var_maker(q, "sync").
ss_ok("ret", g, "") :- ss_sync(g), ss_returns_ok(g).
ss_ok("retcm", g, "") :- ss_sync(g), ss_returns_ok(g), ss_cm(g).

// ss_need(e): an expression whose session the rule asks for: a session method's receiver, a call's argument, a value
// a def binds, an attribute's or a `.state.<a>`'s assigned value.
.decl ss_need(e: node)
ss_need(r) :- ss_recv(_, r, _).
ss_need(a) :- kind(c, "call"), call_target(c, _), call_arg(c, _, _, a0), unparen(a0, a).
ss_need(v) :- fa_bind(h, _, v), kind(h, "function_definition").
ss_need(r) :- assigned_attr(_, "self", _, r0), unparen(r0, r).
ss_need(r) :- ss_state_asg(_, r).
// ss_ec(e, c1, c2, c3): expression e holds a sync session: a name of a def that holds one (ss_name_ok), `self.a`/
// `cls.a` or `K.a` for a class attribute a holding one (ss_class_attr), or `<x>.state.a` when the run assigns a session
// to `.state.a`.
.decl ss_ec(e: node, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_ec(e, "name", sq, x) :- ss_need(e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x), look(e, x, s), kind(s, "function_definition"),
    pt_def(s, sq).
ss_ec(e, "attr", kq, a) :- ss_need(e), attr_of(e, o, a), kind(o, "identifier"), (text(o, "self") ; text(o, "cls")),
    text(o, y), look(o, y, m), nearest(m, k, scope), class_def(k, kq).
ss_ec(e, "attr", q, a) :- ss_need(e), attr_of(e, o, a), sym_of(o, q).
ss_ec(e, "state", a, "") :- ss_need(e), attr_of(e, s, a), attr_of(s, _, "state").
// ss_mk(v, c1, c2, c3): call v makes a sync session (lib/fastapi's fa_session_maker and fa_maker_ext; a maker built
// inline, `sessionmaker(bind=e)()`), or surely calls a sync def that gives one (ss_returns_ok).
.decl ss_mk(v: node, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_mk(v, "sure", "", "") :- fa_session_maker(v, "sync").
ss_mk(v, "maker", q, "") :- fa_maker_ext(v, q).
ss_mk(v, "ret", g, "") :- kind(v, "call"), !call_open(v), call_target(v, g).
// A @contextmanager def is the call's target, with the call open (the decorator is outside the run).
ss_mk(v, "retcm", g, "") :- kind(v, "call"), call_target(v, g).
// ss_cm(g): def g is decorated with contextlib.contextmanager. Stated in its file.
.decl ss_cm(g: symbol)
ss_cm(gq) :- decorator(g, e), unparen(e, m), sym_of(m, "contextlib.contextmanager"), pt_def(g, gq).
// ss_ty(t, c1, c2, c3): type expression t names a sync session class: directly (lib/fastapi's fa_session_type, or
// fa_session_type_ext for an alias of another module), through ClassVar, or through a module alias of this file.
.decl ss_ty(t: node, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_ty(t, "sure", "", "") :- fa_session_type(t, "sync").
ss_ty(t, "type", q, "") :- fa_session_type_ext(t, q).
ss_ty(t, c1, c2, c3) :- fa_sub(t, q), (q = "typing.ClassVar" ; q = "typing_extensions.ClassVar"), fa_sub_arg(t, 0, a),
    ss_ty(a, c1, c2, c3).
ss_ty(t, c1, c2, c3) :- fa_value(t, v), fa_sub(v, _), ss_ty(v, c1, c2, c3).
ss_ty(t, c1, c2, c3) :- fa_strip(t, m), m != t, ss_ty(m, c1, c2, c3).

// ss_name_ok(h, x): in def h, the name x holds a sync session.
.decl ss_name_ok(h: symbol, x: symbol)
// The request's session, from the parameter's type or its dependency.
ss_name_ok(h, x) :- fa_session_param(h, x, "sync").
ss_name_ok(h, x) :- ss_name_src(h, x, c1, c2, c3), ss_ok(c1, c2, c3).
// A parameter some caller passes a session to (ss_pass_at, stated in the caller's file; ss_pos_param and
// ss_kw_param, in h's).
ss_name_ok(h, x) :- ss_pass_at(h, j, "", c1, c2, c3), ss_pos_param(h, j, x), ss_ok(c1, c2, c3).
ss_name_ok(h, x) :- ss_pass_at(h, -1, x, c1, c2, c3), ss_kw_param(h, x), ss_ok(c1, c2, c3).
// ss_name_src(h, x, c1, c2, c3): a parameter of h annotated as a sync session; a session h opens (`x =
// SessionLocal()`, `with Session(engine) as x`, `x = open_session()`); or a local alias of a session.
.decl ss_name_src(h: symbol, x: symbol, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_name_src(hq, x, c1, c2, c3) :- fa_param_type(h, _, x, t), ss_ty(t, c1, c2, c3), pt_def(h, hq).
ss_name_src(hq, x, c1, c2, c3) :- fa_bind(h, x, v), kind(h, "function_definition"), ss_mk(v, c1, c2, c3),
    pt_def(h, hq).
ss_name_src(hq, x, c1, c2, c3) :- fa_bind(h, x, v), kind(h, "function_definition"), ss_ec(v, c1, c2, c3),
    pt_def(h, hq).
ss_name_src(hq, x, c1, c2, c3) :- ss_with(w, x, c1, c2, c3), nearest(w, h, ss_stop), kind(h, "function_definition"),
    pt_def(h, hq).
// ss_with(w, x, c1, c2, c3): with-statement w binds x to the session its item makes (`with SessionLocal() as x`,
// `with session_scope() as x`).
.decl ss_with(w: node, x: symbol, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_with(w, x, c1, c2, c3) :- kind(w, "with_statement"), child(w, wc, _), kind(wc, "with_clause"), child(wc, wi, _),
    kind(wi, "with_item"), field(wi, "value", ap), kind(ap, "as_pattern"), child(ap, v0, 0), unparen(v0, v),
    ss_mk(v, c1, c2, c3), field(ap, "alias", t), child(t, n, 0), kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, x).
ss_with(w, x, c1, c2, c3) :- kind(w, "with_statement"), child(w, wc, _), kind(wc, "with_clause"), child(wc, wi, _),
    kind(wi, "with_item"), field(wi, "value", ap), kind(ap, "as_pattern"), child(ap, v0, 0), unparen(v0, v),
    ss_mk(v, c1, c2, c3), field(ap, "alias", t), kind(t, "identifier"), text(t, x).

// ss_pass_at(h, j, x, c1, c2, c3): a call whose target is h passes a sync session, positionally (j its place, x "")
// or by keyword x (j -1).
.decl ss_pass_at(h: symbol, j: number, x: symbol, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_pass_at(h, j, "", c1, c2, c3) :- call_target(c, h), call_arg(c, j, "", a0), j >= 0, unparen(a0, a),
    ss_ec(a, c1, c2, c3).
ss_pass_at(h, -1, x, c1, c2, c3) :- call_target(c, h), call_arg(c, -1, x, a0), x != "", unparen(a0, a),
    ss_ec(a, c1, c2, c3).
// ss_pos_param(h, j, x): the j-th positional argument of a call of def h fills its parameter x, past a method's self
// or cls (ss_offset). ss_kw_param(h, x): h has a parameter x.
.decl ss_pos_param(h: symbol, j: number, x: symbol)
ss_pos_param(hq, j, x) :- ss_offset(h, n), sig_param(h, _, nm, i, k, _, _), (k = "pos" ; k = "posonly"), text(nm, x),
    j = i - n, j >= 0, pt_def(h, hq).
.decl ss_kw_param(h: symbol, x: symbol)
ss_kw_param(hq, x) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), param_named(h, x, _), pt_def(h, hq).
// ss_offset(h, n): a call's first positional argument fills h's parameter n: 1 for a method's self or cls.
.decl ss_offset(h: node, n: number)
ss_offset(h, 1) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), nearest(h, k, scope), kind(k, "class_definition"), !ss_static(h).
ss_offset(h, 0) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), nearest(h, k, scope), kind(k, "class_definition"), ss_static(h).
ss_offset(h, 0) :- kind(h, "function_definition"), nearest(h, k, scope), !kind(k, "class_definition").
.decl ss_static(h: node)
ss_static(h) :- decorator(h, e), unparen(e, m), sym_of(m, "staticmethod").
ss_static(h) :- decorator(h, e), unparen(e, m), kind(m, "identifier"), text(m, "staticmethod").

// ss_returns_ok(g): def g returns or yields a sync session: its return annotation names one (`-> Session`,
// `-> Iterator[Session]` on a @contextmanager), or it returns or yields a session it makes or holds (ss_ret_src,
// stated in g's file).
.decl ss_returns_ok(g: symbol)
ss_returns_ok(g) :- ss_ret_src(g, c1, c2, c3), ss_ok(c1, c2, c3).
.decl ss_ret_src(g: symbol, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_ret_src(gq, c1, c2, c3) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), field(g, "return_type", rt0), fa_strip(rt0, rt),
    ss_ty(rt, c1, c2, c3), pt_def(g, gq).
ss_ret_src(gq, c1, c2, c3) :- fa_gives(g, e), ss_mk(e, c1, c2, c3), pt_def(g, gq).
ss_ret_src(gq, "name", gq, x) :- fa_gives(g, e), kind(e, "identifier"), text(e, x), pt_def(g, gq).

// ss_class_attr(q, a): class q, or one of its bases, has attribute a holding a sync session. ss_attr_src(q, a, c1,
// c2, c3): q declares a as one (`session: ClassVar[SessionType]`, `session: Session`), or one of its methods assigns
// `self.a` one (`self.session = session` with `session: Session`); stated in q's file.
.decl ss_attr_src(q: symbol, a: symbol, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_attr_src(q, a, c1, c2, c3) :- class_def(c, q), field(c, "body", b), child(b, s, _), kind(s, "expression_statement"),
    child(s, n, 0), kind(n, "assignment"), field(n, "left", l), kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, a), field(n, "type", t0),
    fa_strip(t0, t), ss_ty(t, c1, c2, c3).
ss_attr_src(q, a, c1, c2, c3) :- assigned_attr(m, "self", a, r0), unparen(r0, r), ss_ec(r, c1, c2, c3),
    nearest(m, c, scope), class_def(c, q).
ss_attr_src(q, a, c1, c2, c3) :- assigned_attr(m, "self", a, r0), unparen(r0, r), ss_mk(r, c1, c2, c3),
    nearest(m, c, scope), class_def(c, q).
.decl ss_attr_ok(q: symbol, a: symbol)
ss_attr_ok(q, a) :- ss_attr_src(q, a, c1, c2, c3), ss_ok(c1, c2, c3).
.decl ss_class_attr(q: symbol, a: symbol)
ss_class_attr(q, a) :- ss_attr_ok(q, a).
ss_class_attr(q, a) :- ss_super(q, b), ss_attr_ok(b, a).

// ss_state_ok(a): the run assigns a sync session to `<x>.state.a` (`request.state.db = SessionLocal()`).
.decl ss_state_asg(a: symbol, r: node)
ss_state_asg(a, r) :- kind(n, "assignment"), field(n, "left", l), attr_of(l, s, a), attr_of(s, _, "state"),
    field(n, "right", r0), fa_unwrap(r0, r).
.decl ss_state_src(a: symbol, c1: symbol, c2: symbol, c3: symbol)
ss_state_src(a, c1, c2, c3) :- ss_state_asg(a, r), ss_mk(r, c1, c2, c3).
ss_state_src(a, c1, c2, c3) :- ss_state_asg(a, r), ss_ec(r, c1, c2, c3).
.decl ss_state_ok(a: symbol)
ss_state_ok(a) :- ss_state_src(a, c1, c2, c3), ss_ok(c1, c2, c3).

